VALUES
('handling-a-biting-toddler-without-the-overwhelm', 'Handling a Biting Toddler Without the Overwhelm', 'There''s a version of handling a biting toddler that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough t', 'Daniel Okafor', '2026-03-26', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#parenting','#handlingbiting','#familytime','#dadlife']::text[], 'Parenting', false, '#7c5dff', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"There's a version of handling a biting toddler that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. This is about getting to the second one."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Give the choice, keep the frame"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Bath now or after this show?\" beats \"Go take a bath.\" The child gets agency; you keep the outcome. It's the oldest trick in the parenting book because it works."},{"type":"h2","text":"Lower the bar on purpose"},{"type":"p","text":"Perfectionism is the enemy of a warm home. A \"good enough\" dinner eaten together beats a Pinterest meal served to a stressed-out table."},{"type":"h2","text":"Name the feeling before the fix"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids (and adults) calm down when they feel understood, not when they're handed a solution. A quick \"you really wanted more time, huh?\" lands better than a lecture. With handling a biting toddler, naming the emotion first buys you the cooperation the logic needs."},{"type":"h2","text":"Model the repair, not just the rule"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids do as we do far more than as we say. If you want calm, be calm out loud: \"I'm taking a breath because I'm frustrated\" is a masterclass they'll remember."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, write down the plan so it survives a chaotic day. Next, start smaller than feels necessary — momentum beats ambition. Then, put it somewhere the whole family can see it."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"Bubaly was designed for moments exactly like this: it takes handling a biting toddler off your mental to-do list and turns it into shared, automatic routines the whole family can see. Learn more at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"You'll still have messy days. That's fine. A good routine bends without breaking."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
('winning-at-the-gentle-approach-to-night-weaning-on-a-normal-week', 'Winning at The Gentle Approach to Night Weaning on a Normal Week', 'Ask ten parents about the gentle approach to night weaning and you''ll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh. What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: sim', 'Elena Rossi', '2026-04-16', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#parenting','#gentleapproach','#organizedhome','#dadlife']::text[], 'Parenting', false, '#7c5dff', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Ask ten parents about the gentle approach to night weaning and you'll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Routines beat reminders"},{"type":"p","text":"A predictable sequence — same steps, same order — means you stop being the nag and the routine becomes the boss. Kids resist people; they rarely resist a chart they helped make."},{"type":"h2","text":"Repair is the real lesson"},{"type":"p","text":"You will lose your temper. The magic isn't never rupturing — it's the repair afterward. \"I was frustrated and I snapped; that wasn't fair\" teaches more about relationships than a hundred calm days."},{"type":"h2","text":"One-on-one beats the group"},{"type":"p","text":"Even a quick errand run solo with one child fills a cup that group time can't reach. Rotate who gets the passenger seat and watch the rivalry cool."},{"type":"h2","text":"Model the repair, not just the rule"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids do as we do far more than as we say. If you want calm, be calm out loud: \"I'm taking a breath because I'm frustrated\" is a masterclass they'll remember."},{"type":"h2","text":"Connection before correction"},{"type":"p","text":"Behavior is communication. A ten-second reconnect — eye level, a hand on the shoulder, a real question — resolves more than a raised voice ever will, and it costs almost nothing."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, decide the one default that removes a daily decision. Next, add a gentle reminder so nobody has to hold it in their head. Then, pick the single piece of the gentle approach to night weaning that causes the most friction this week."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"If keeping the gentle approach to night weaning on track sounds exhausting, that's the point where Bubaly quietly helps. It's the AI operating system for family life — it remembers, reminds, and coordinates so you don't have to carry it all alone. See how at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"None of this has to be perfect. Pick one idea, try it for a week, and keep only what earns its place."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
('a-simple-system-for-helping-kids-share-without-forcing-it', 'A Simple System for Helping Kids Share without Forcing It', 'The secret to helping kids share without forcing it isn''t more willpower. Here''s the framework, the small habits that make it stick, and the honest caveats nobody mentions.', 'Sofia Alvarez', '2026-05-08', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#parenting','#helpingkids','#dadlife','#lifehacks']::text[], 'Parenting', false, '#7c5dff', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"The secret to helping kids share without forcing it isn't more willpower. It's less friction — fewer decisions, clearer defaults, and a plan everyone can see."},{"type":"p","text":"Here's the framework, the small habits that make it stick, and the honest caveats nobody mentions."},{"type":"h2","text":"Catch them being good"},{"type":"p","text":"Attention is fertilizer; whatever you water grows. Narrate the small wins — \"you put your shoes away without me asking\" — and you'll see more of them."},{"type":"h2","text":"Model the repair, not just the rule"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids do as we do far more than as we say. If you want calm, be calm out loud: \"I'm taking a breath because I'm frustrated\" is a masterclass they'll remember."},{"type":"h2","text":"Protect the wind-down"},{"type":"p","text":"The hour before bed sets the tone for the night and the morning after. Dimmer lights, lower voices, and screens away make sleep arrive on its own instead of by force."},{"type":"h2","text":"Special time, protected"},{"type":"p","text":"Ten minutes of undivided, child-led attention a day does more for behavior than an hour of correction. Put it on the calendar so it survives busy weeks."},{"type":"h2","text":"One-on-one beats the group"},{"type":"p","text":"Even a quick errand run solo with one child fills a cup that group time can't reach. Rotate who gets the passenger seat and watch the rivalry cool."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, decide the one default that removes a daily decision. Next, start smaller than feels necessary — momentum beats ambition. Then, write down the plan so it survives a chaotic day."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"Bubaly was designed for moments exactly like this: it takes helping kids share without forcing it off your mental to-do list and turns it into shared, automatic routines the whole family can see. Learn more at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"You'll still have messy days. That's fine. A good routine bends without breaking."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
('everything-families-get-wrong-about-raising-a-strong-willed-toddler', 'Everything Families Get Wrong About Raising a Strong-willed Toddler', 'Most families don''t struggle with raising a strong-willed toddler because they''re doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system. Below is a calm, practical way', 'Priya Nair', '2026-05-24', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#parenting','#raisingstrongwilled','#familyfirst','#parentinghacks']::text[], 'Parenting', false, '#7c5dff', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Most families don't struggle with raising a strong-willed toddler because they're doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system."},{"type":"p","text":"Below is a calm, practical way to think about it — not a rigid program, just a handful of ideas you can borrow tonight and adjust for your own family."},{"type":"h2","text":"Lower the bar on purpose"},{"type":"p","text":"Perfectionism is the enemy of a warm home. A \"good enough\" dinner eaten together beats a Pinterest meal served to a stressed-out table."},{"type":"h2","text":"Consistency over intensity"},{"type":"p","text":"A quiet rule kept every day outperforms a dramatic one kept once. Kids are scientists; they run experiments on our boundaries, and steadiness gives them the answer faster than volume."},{"type":"h2","text":"Let them be bored"},{"type":"p","text":"Boredom is the doorway to imagination. Resisting the urge to fill every gap teaches kids to generate their own fun — a skill worth more than any enrichment class."},{"type":"h2","text":"Say yes in spirit"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Yes, and we'll do it Saturday\" honors the want without breaking the boundary. Kids can wait; what they can't stand is feeling unheard."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, pick the single piece of raising a strong-willed toddler that causes the most friction this week. Next, start smaller than feels necessary — momentum beats ambition. Then, give it two weeks before you judge whether it's working."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"Want raising a strong-willed toddler to run itself? That's what Bubaly does — one calm home for your family's schedule, tasks, meals, and money, with AI that stays a step ahead. Start at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"You'll still have messy days. That's fine. A good routine bends without breaking."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
