('how-to-handle-building-a-calm-down-corner-that-works-and-actually-enjoy-it', 'How to Handle Building a Calm-down Corner that Works (and Actually Enjoy It)', 'Ask ten parents about building a calm-down corner that works and you''ll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh. We''ll walk through what actually moves the needle, wha', 'Sofia Alvarez', '2024-02-03', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#parenting','#buildingcalmdown','#organizedhome','#homelife']::text[], 'Parenting', false, '#7c5dff', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Ask ten parents about building a calm-down corner that works and you'll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh."},{"type":"p","text":"We'll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip, and how to make it feel less like a chore and more like a shared routine."},{"type":"h2","text":"Repair is the real lesson"},{"type":"p","text":"You will lose your temper. The magic isn't never rupturing — it's the repair afterward. \"I was frustrated and I snapped; that wasn't fair\" teaches more about relationships than a hundred calm days."},{"type":"h2","text":"The 2-minute head start"},{"type":"p","text":"Transitions are where meltdowns live. A gentle countdown — \"two more minutes, then we clean up\" — respects a child's need to finish a thought and heads off half your battles."},{"type":"h2","text":"Let them be bored"},{"type":"p","text":"Boredom is the doorway to imagination. Resisting the urge to fill every gap teaches kids to generate their own fun — a skill worth more than any enrichment class."},{"type":"h2","text":"Say yes in spirit"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Yes, and we'll do it Saturday\" honors the want without breaking the boundary. Kids can wait; what they can't stand is feeling unheard."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, pick the single piece of building a calm-down corner that works that causes the most friction this week. Next, agree on who owns it so it isn't quietly one person's job. Then, add a gentle reminder so nobody has to hold it in their head."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"This is exactly the kind of invisible work Bubaly was built for. Instead of holding building a calm-down corner that works in your head, you hand it to your family's shared system — Bubaly turns plans into real calendar events, reminders, lists, and gentle nudges, so the whole household stays in sync. Explore it at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"You'll still have messy days. That's fine. A good routine bends without breaking."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
('winning-at-helping-kids-with-separation-at-bedtime-on-a-normal-week', 'Winning at Helping Kids with Separation At Bedtime on a Normal Week', 'The secret to helping kids with separation at bedtime isn''t more willpower. What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough t', 'Nina Patel', '2024-02-21', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#parenting','#helpingkids','#familytime','#parentinghacks']::text[], 'Parenting', false, '#7c5dff', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"The secret to helping kids with separation at bedtime isn't more willpower. It's less friction — fewer decisions, clearer defaults, and a plan everyone can see."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"One-on-one beats the group"},{"type":"p","text":"Even a quick errand run solo with one child fills a cup that group time can't reach. Rotate who gets the passenger seat and watch the rivalry cool."},{"type":"h2","text":"Name the feeling before the fix"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids (and adults) calm down when they feel understood, not when they're handed a solution. A quick \"you really wanted more time, huh?\" lands better than a lecture. With helping kids with separation at bedtime, naming the emotion first buys you the cooperation the logic needs."},{"type":"h2","text":"Consistency over intensity"},{"type":"p","text":"A quiet rule kept every day outperforms a dramatic one kept once. Kids are scientists; they run experiments on our boundaries, and steadiness gives them the answer faster than volume."},{"type":"h2","text":"The 2-minute head start"},{"type":"p","text":"Transitions are where meltdowns live. A gentle countdown — \"two more minutes, then we clean up\" — respects a child's need to finish a thought and heads off half your battles."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First,