('rethinking-teaching-kids-about-personal-space-for-the-modern-family', 'Rethinking Teaching Kids About Personal Space for the Modern Family', 'The secret to teaching kids about personal space isn''t more willpower. Here''s the framework, the small habits that make it stick, and the honest caveats nobody mentions.', 'Jessica Miller', '2025-03-27', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#parenting','#teachingkids','#raisingkids','#organizedhome']::text[], 'Parenting', false, '#7c5dff', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"The secret to teaching kids about personal space isn't more willpower. It's less friction — fewer decisions, clearer defaults, and a plan everyone can see."},{"type":"p","text":"Here's the framework, the small habits that make it stick, and the honest caveats nobody mentions."},{"type":"h2","text":"Model the repair, not just the rule"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids do as we do far more than as we say. If you want calm, be calm out loud: \"I'm taking a breath because I'm frustrated\" is a masterclass they'll remember."},{"type":"h2","text":"Lower the bar on purpose"},{"type":"p","text":"Perfectionism is the enemy of a warm home. A \"good enough\" dinner eaten together beats a Pinterest meal served to a stressed-out table."},{"type":"h2","text":"Praise the effort, not the trait"},{"type":"p","text":"\"You worked hard on that\" grows a child who tries; \"you're so smart\" grows one who fears being wrong. The words are small; the difference compounds for years."},{"type":"h2","text":"Siblings: coach, don't referee"},{"type":"p","text":"Stepping in to declare a winner teaches kids to recruit you as a weapon. Narrating both sides and handing the problem back — \"you two figure out a fair turn\" — builds the skill that actually ends the fighting."},{"type":"h2","text":"Say yes in spirit"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Yes, and we'll do it Saturday\" honors the want without breaking the boundary. Kids can wait; what they can't stand is feeling unheard."},{"type":"h2"