('organizing-kids-art-supplies-by-project-without-the-overwhelm', 'Organizing Kids'' Art Supplies By Project Without the Overwhelm', 'Most families don''t struggle with organizing kids'' art supplies by project because they''re doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system. What follows is the a', 'Elena Rossi', '2026-06-11', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familyorganization','#organizingkids','#familytime','#homelife']::text[], 'Organization', false, '#3b82f6', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Most families don't struggle with organizing kids' art supplies by project because they're doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"A home for everything"},{"type":"p","text":"Clutter is mostly deferred decisions. When keys, backpacks, and permission slips each have one obvious home, tidying stops being a project and becomes a reflex. Start organizing kids' art supplies by project by deciding where things live."},{"type":"h2","text":"Make the default visible"},{"type":"p","text":"A checklist taped where the task happens — the morning routine on the fridge, the packing list by the door — outsources your memory to the wall and ends the reminding."},{"type":"h2","text":"One in, one out"},{"type":"p","text":"The fastest way to keep clutter from creeping back is a quiet trade: a new toy in, an old one out. It keeps volume flat without a single big purge."},{"type":"h2","text":"Launch pad by the door"},{"type":"p","text":"A single spot where everything that leaves the house lives — bags, shoes, water bottles, signed forms — turns frantic mornings into a grab-and-go. What's not on the launch pad doesn't make it out."},{"type":"h2","text":"Declutter by the surface, not the house"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Organize the house\" is a project you'll never s