('the-first-week-of-kindergarten-made-easy', 'The First Week of Kindergarten, Made Easy', 'The First Week of Kindergarten is one of those quietly relentless parts of family life: never urgent enough to fix, never small enough to ignore. We''ll walk through what actually m', 'Daniel Okafor', '2024-01-25', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#schoollife','#firstweek','#familyfirst','#worklifebalance']::text[], 'School & Activities', false, '#10b981', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"The First Week of Kindergarten is one of those quietly relentless parts of family life: never urgent enough to fix, never small enough to ignore."},{"type":"p","text":"We'll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip, and how to make it feel less like a chore and more like a shared routine."},{"type":"h2","text":"Read the newsletter for two facts"},{"type":"p","text":"School emails are warm, long, and mostly context. Skim for the two things that need an action — a date, a form — and turn each into a calendar event before you close the tab."},{"type":"h2","text":"Talk to the teacher early"},{"type":"p","text":"A friendly note in week two beats a tense meeting in month three. Teachers are allies; the earlier you're on the same page, the smaller every problem stays."},{"type":"h2","text":"Keep a supplies stash"},{"type":"p","text":"Nothing derails a school night like a missing poster board at 8pm. A small, replenished stash of the usual suspects saves a hundred emergency store runs."},{"type":"h2","text":"The after-school reset"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids come home with a full cup of held-together effort. A snack, some downtime, and no interrogation before homework respects the crash — and prevents the meltdown."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, add a gentle reminder so nobody has to hold it in their head. Next, agree on who owns it so it isn't quietly one person's job. Then, write down the plan so it survives a chaotic day."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"If keeping the first week of kindergarten on track sounds exhausting, that's the point where Bubaly quietly helps. It's the AI operating system for family life — it remembers, reminds, and coordinates so you don't have to carry it all alone. See how at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"None of this has to be perfect. Pick one idea, try it for a week, and keep only what earns its place."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
('helping-a-kid-who-forgets-their-homework-what-really-works-for-busy-families', 'Helping a Kid Who Forgets Their Homework: What Really Works for Busy Families', 'There''s a version of helping a kid who forgets their homework that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. We''ll walk through what actually moves the needle, wh', 'The Bubaly Team', '2024-02-07', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#schoollife','#helpingforgets','#organizedhome','#worklifebalance']::text[], 'School & Activities', false, '#10b981', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"There's a version of helping a kid who forgets their homework that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. This is about getting to the second one."},{"type":"p","text":"We'll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip, and how to make it feel less like a chore and more like a shared routine."},{"type":"h2","text":"Pack the night before"},{"type":"p","text":"Mornings are for leaving, not deciding. Bags packed, clothes out, lunches half-made the night before turns the school run from a sprint into a walk."},{"type":"h2","text":"Read the newsletter for two facts"},{"type":"p","text":"School emails are warm, long, and mostly context. Skim for the two things that need an action — a date, a form — and turn each into a calendar event before you close the tab."},{"type":"h2","text":"Celebrate effort over grades"},{"type":"p","text":"Praising the studying, not the score, grows a kid who keeps trying when it gets hard. The grade is a snapshot; the effort is the skill."},{"type":"h2","text":"Homework has a time and a place"},{"type":"p","text":"A consistent when and where beats nagging every night. Same table, same hour, supplies already there — the routine carries the willpower so your child doesn't have to."},{"type":"h2","text":"Don't do the homework"},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is a capable kid, not a finished worksheet. \"Quiz me,\" \"explain it back,\" and \"where ar