('the-quiet-art-of-the-science-fair-project-timeline', 'The Quiet Art of The Science-fair Project Timeline', 'There''s a version of the science-fair project timeline that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple ', 'Jessica Miller', '2024-03-11', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#schoollife','#sciencefairproject','#parentinghacks','#momlife']::text[], 'School & Activities', false, '#10b981', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"There's a version of the science-fair project timeline that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. This is about getting to the second one."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Celebrate effort over grades"},{"type":"p","text":"Praising the studying, not the score, grows a kid who keeps trying when it gets hard. The grade is a snapshot; the effort is the skill."},{"type":"h2","text":"Track the big rocks only"},{"type":"p","text":"You don't need to manage every quiz. Keep an eye on the projects, the tests, and the due dates that matter, and let the daily small stuff belong to your child."},{"type":"h2","text":"Talk to the teacher early"},{"type":"p","text":"A friendly note in week two beats a tense meeting in month three. Teachers are allies; the earlier you're on the same page, the smaller every problem stays."},{"type":"h2","text":"Keep a supplies stash"},{"type":"p","text":"Nothing derails a school night like a missing poster board at 8pm. A small, replenished stash of the usual suspects saves a hundred emergency store runs."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, decide the one default that removes a daily decision. Next, pick the single piece of the science-fair project timeline that causes the most friction this week. Then, start smaller than feels necessary — 