('the-summer-reading-plan-that-sticks-what-really-works-for-busy-families', 'The Summer Reading Plan that Sticks: What Really Works for Busy Families', 'There''s a version of the summer reading plan that sticks that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. We''ll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to', 'The Bubaly Team', '2024-10-21', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#schoollife','#summerreading','#dadlife','#familyfirst']::text[], 'School & Activities', false, '#10b981', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"There's a version of the summer reading plan that sticks that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. This is about getting to the second one."},{"type":"p","text":"We'll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip, and how to make it feel less like a chore and more like a shared routine."},{"type":"h2","text":"Read the newsletter for two facts"},{"type":"p","text":"School emails are warm, long, and mostly context. Skim for the two things that need an action — a date, a form — and turn each into a calendar event before you close the tab."},{"type":"h2","text":"A visible countdown to due dates"},{"type":"p","text":"Big projects sink kids because \"next week\" isn't real to them. A visible countdown broken into small steps turns a scary deadline into a series of easy Tuesdays."},{"type":"h2","text":"Talk to the teacher early"},{"type":"p","text":"A friendly note in week two beats a tense meeting in month three. Teachers are allies; the earlier you're on the same page, the smaller every problem stays."},{"type":"h2","text":"Protect the sleep, guard the mornings"},{"type":"p","text":"Nearly every school-morning battle traces back to bedtime the night before. Win the evening and the morning mostly wins itself."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, start smaller than feels necessary — momentum beats ambition. Next, agree on who owns it so it isn't quietly