('everything-families-get-wrong-about-supporting-a-gifted-kid-who-is-bored', 'Everything Families Get Wrong About Supporting a Gifted Kid Who Is Bored', 'Ask ten parents about supporting a gifted kid who is bored and you''ll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh. Below is a calm, practical way to think about it — not a', 'Hannah Cho', '2026-07-01', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#schoollife','#supportinggifted','#lifehacks','#parentinghacks']::text[], 'School & Activities', false, '#10b981', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Ask ten parents about supporting a gifted kid who is bored and you'll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh."},{"type":"p","text":"Below is a calm, practical way to think about it — not a rigid program, just a handful of ideas you can borrow tonight and adjust for your own family."},{"type":"h2","text":"Talk to the teacher early"},{"type":"p","text":"A friendly note in week two beats a tense meeting in month three. Teachers are allies; the earlier you're on the same page, the smaller every problem stays."},{"type":"h2","text":"Track the big rocks only"},{"type":"p","text":"You don't need to manage every quiz. Keep an eye on the projects, the tests, and the due dates that matter, and let the daily small stuff belong to your child."},{"type":"h2","text":"Celebrate effort over grades"},{"type":"p","text":"Praising the studying, not the score, grows a kid who keeps trying when it gets hard. The grade is a snapshot; the effort is the skill."},{"type":"h2","text":"Protect the sleep, guard the mornings"},{"type":"p","text":"Nearly every school-morning battle traces back to bedtime the night before. Win the evening and the morning mostly wins itself."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, add a gentle reminder so nobody has to hold it in their head. Next, give it two weeks before you judge whether it's working. Then, pick the single piece of supporting a gifted kid who is b