('using-ai-to-plan-a-birthday-scavenger-hunt-that-actually-sticks', 'Using AI to Plan a Birthday Scavenger Hunt That Actually Sticks', 'If using AI to plan a birthday scavenger hunt has ever turned an ordinary evening into a low-grade negotiation, you are in excellent company. We''ll walk through what actually moves', 'Jessica Miller', '2024-04-21', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familytech','#usingplan','#dadlife','#worklifebalance']::text[], 'AI & Technology', false, '#6366f1', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"If using AI to plan a birthday scavenger hunt has ever turned an ordinary evening into a low-grade negotiation, you are in excellent company."},{"type":"p","text":"We'll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip, and how to make it feel less like a chore and more like a shared routine."},{"type":"h2","text":"The school-email translator"},{"type":"p","text":"AI is very good at pulling the two actionable facts out of a 400-word newsletter and turning them into a reminder and an event. It's the closest thing to a personal secretary a busy parent will ever get."},{"type":"h2","text":"Screens with intention"},{"type":"p","text":"The problem was never screens; it's aimless screens. Tools that default to a plan — homework help that doesn't do the homework, timers that end gently — turn a fight into a feature."},{"type":"h2","text":"Privacy is a feature, not a footnote"},{"type":"p","text":"A family's data is uniquely sensitive. Before you adopt any tool, ask where the data lives, who can see it, and how you delete it. Good answers are a green light; vague ones are an exit."},{"type":"h2","text":"Guardrails for kids"},{"type":"p","text":"The right setup gives kids room to explore with rails, not a locked door. Age-appropriate limits, transparent history, and conversations beat surveillance every time."},{"type":"h2","text":"Trust is a dial, not a switch"},{"type":"p","text":"Nobody should hand their household to an algorithm on day on