('everything-families-get-wrong-about-building-a-screen-free-bedtime-for-kids', 'Everything Families Get Wrong About Building a Screen-free Bedtime for Kids', 'Nobody puts building a screen-free bedtime for kids on their vision board, and yet it shapes the temperature of the whole house. What follows is the approach we keep coming back to', 'Daniel Okafor', '2024-05-10', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familywellness','#buildingscreenfree','#organizedhome','#parentinghacks']::text[], 'Wellness', false, '#f59e0b', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Nobody puts building a screen-free bedtime for kids on their vision board, and yet it shapes the temperature of the whole house."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Connection is medicine"},{"type":"p","text":"Loneliness is a health risk; belonging is a buffer. Regular, low-stakes togetherness — a shared meal, a standing walk — does quiet, measurable good for everyone under the roof."},{"type":"h2","text":"Hydration and the afternoon slump"},{"type":"p","text":"Half of the 4pm meltdown — kids and adults — is really hunger and thirst wearing a costume. A snack and a glass of water resolve more than a timeout ever will."},{"type":"h2","text":"Less news, more presence"},{"type":"p","text":"A household marinating in headlines carries a background hum of dread. Curating the input — and being present instead of scrolling — lowers the whole family's baseline stress."},{"type":"h2","text":"Small rituals, big anchors"},{"type":"p","text":"A Friday movie night or a Sunday pancake breakfast gives the week a shape to lean on. Rituals cost little and return a sense of steadiness kids remember for decades."},{"type":"h2","text":"Breathe before you react"},{"type":"p","text":"One slow breath creates a gap between the trigger and the response, and in that gap lives every good parenting deci