('a-simple-system-for-a-family-plan-for-protecting-downtime', 'A Simple System for A Family Plan for Protecting Downtime', 'There''s a version of a family plan for protecting downtime that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. Here''s the framework, the small habits that make it stic', 'The Bubaly Team', '2025-09-30', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familywellness','#familyplan','#organizedhome','#homelife']::text[], 'Wellness', false, '#f59e0b', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"There's a version of a family plan for protecting downtime that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. This is about getting to the second one."},{"type":"p","text":"Here's the framework, the small habits that make it stick, and the honest caveats nobody mentions."},{"type":"h2","text":"The 80/20 plate"},{"type":"p","text":"Nutrition isn't all-or-nothing. Aim for mostly-good most of the time and let dessert be dessert. The pressure to be perfect causes more harm at the table than the occasional cookie."},{"type":"h2","text":"Sunlight and outside time"},{"type":"p","text":"Ten minutes of morning light sets the body clock; time outdoors resets the mood. It's free, it's fast, and it does more for the whole family than most supplements."},{"type":"h2","text":"Move together, not perfectly"},{"type":"p","text":"A walk after dinner beats a gym membership nobody uses. Movement that's woven into family life — a bike ride, a dance-off, raking leaves — sticks because it's shared and fun."},{"type":"h2","text":"Feelings need words"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids who can name what they feel can manage it. A simple daily check-in — rose, thorn, bud — builds emotional vocabulary that pays off for a lifetime."},{"type":"h2","text":"Protect white space"},{"type":"p","text":"An over-scheduled family is a stressed family. Guarding a few blank evenings a week isn't laziness; it's maintenance. Rest is where the recovery actually happens."},{"type":"h2","text":