('rethinking-helping-kids-build-a-bedtime-they-own-for-the-modern-family', 'Rethinking Helping Kids Build a Bedtime They Own for the Modern Family', 'If helping kids build a bedtime they own has ever turned an ordinary evening into a low-grade negotiation, you are in excellent company. What follows is the approach we keep coming', 'The Bubaly Team', '2024-06-09', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familywellness','#helpingkids','#parentinghacks','#organizedhome']::text[], 'Wellness', false, '#f59e0b', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"If helping kids build a bedtime they own has ever turned an ordinary evening into a low-grade negotiation, you are in excellent company."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Small rituals, big anchors"},{"type":"p","text":"A Friday movie night or a Sunday pancake breakfast gives the week a shape to lean on. Rituals cost little and return a sense of steadiness kids remember for decades."},{"type":"h2","text":"The 80/20 plate"},{"type":"p","text":"Nutrition isn't all-or-nothing. Aim for mostly-good most of the time and let dessert be dessert. The pressure to be perfect causes more harm at the table than the occasional cookie."},{"type":"h2","text":"Breathe before you react"},{"type":"p","text":"One slow breath creates a gap between the trigger and the response, and in that gap lives every good parenting decision you'll ever make. It's the cheapest tool with the highest return."},{"type":"h2","text":"Model the repair with yourself"},{"type":"p","text":"Kids learn self-care by watching. When they see you rest without guilt, apologize without shame, and ask for help without drama, you teach more than any lecture could."},{"type":"h2","text":"Move together, not perfectly"},{"type":"p","text":"A walk after dinner beats a gym membership nobody uses. Movement that's woven into family life — a bike r