('a-simple-system-for-teaching-kids-to-save-a-portion-of-every-gift', 'A Simple System for Teaching Kids to Save a Portion of Every Gift', 'The secret to teaching kids to save a portion of every gift isn''t more willpower. Below is a calm, practical way to think about it — not a rigid program, just a handful of ideas yo', 'The Bubaly Team', '2026-02-12', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familyfinance','#teachingkids','#dadlife','#raisingkids']::text[], 'Family Finances', false, '#ec4899', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"The secret to teaching kids to save a portion of every gift isn't more willpower. It's less friction — fewer decisions, clearer defaults, and a plan everyone can see."},{"type":"p","text":"Below is a calm, practical way to think about it — not a rigid program, just a handful of ideas you can borrow tonight and adjust for your own family."},{"type":"h2","text":"The three-jar system for kids"},{"type":"p","text":"Spend, save, give. Splitting allowance three ways turns an abstract lecture into a hands-on lesson a six-year-old can feel. The jar they watch grow teaches patience better than any talk."},{"type":"h2","text":"Plan for the irregular"},{"type":"p","text":"Holidays, birthdays, and back-to-school aren't surprises — they arrive on schedule every year. Setting aside a little each month means they never blow up the budget."},{"type":"h2","text":"Involve kids in real trade-offs"},{"type":"p","text":"Handing a child the grocery list and a budget teaches more in one trip than a year of lectures. Real choices with real limits build real judgment."},{"type":"h2","text":"Sinking funds beat credit"},{"type":"p","text":"Saving a little each month toward a known future cost — new tires, summer camp — means paying cash for the predictable instead of financing it in a panic."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, pick the single piece of teaching kids to save a portion of every gift that causes the most friction this week. Next, decide the one default that removes a daily decision. Then, write down the plan so it survives a chaotic day."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"If keeping teaching kids to save a portion of every gift on track sounds exhausting, that's the point where Bubaly quietly helps. It's the AI operating system for family life — it remembers, reminds, and coordinates so you don't have to carry it all alone. See how at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"The goal was never a flawless household. It's a calmer one — and that's absolutely within reach."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
('the-honest-guide-to-saving-for-a-first-family-car', 'The Honest Guide to Saving for a First Family Car', 'Ask ten parents about saving for a first family car and you''ll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh. We''ll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip', 'Jessica Miller', '2026-03-07', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familyfinance','#savingfirst','#homelife','#lifehacks']::text[], 'Family Finances', false, '#ec4899', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Ask ten parents about saving for a first family car and you'll get ten answers, forty opinions, and one shared sigh."},{"type":"p","text":"We'll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip, and how to make it feel less like a chore and more like a shared routine."},{"type":"h2","text":"Name the emergency fund"},{"type":"p","text":"A cushion of even a few hundred dollars converts a crisis into an inconvenience. Start absurdly small if you must; the habit matters more than the number at first."},{"type":"h2","text":"Plan for the irregular"},{"type":"p","text":"Holidays, birthdays, and back-to-school aren't surprises — they arrive on schedule every year. Setting aside a little each month means they never blow up the budget."},{"type":"h2","text":"Talk about money openly"},{"type":"p","text":"Money silence is how bad habits get inherited. Age-appropriate honesty — \"we're saving for that, so not this month\" — raises kids who understand trade-offs instead of fearing them."},{"type":"h2","text":"Sinking funds beat credit"},{"type":"p","text":"Saving a little each month toward a known future cost — new tires, summer camp — means paying cash for the predictable instead of financing it in a panic."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, write down the plan so it survives a chaotic day. Next, decide the one default that removes a daily decision. Then, give it two weeks before you judge whether it's working."},{"type":"h2","text"