('the-picky-eater-friendly-stir-fry-that-actually-sticks', 'The Picky-eater-friendly Stir-fry That Actually Sticks', 'There''s a version of the picky-eater-friendly stir-fry that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. Below is a calm, practical way to think about it — not a rig', 'Marcus Bell', '2025-02-25', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familymeals','#pickyeaterfriendlystirfry','#raisingkids','#dadlife']::text[], 'Recipes & Food', false, '#f97316', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"There's a version of the picky-eater-friendly stir-fry that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. This is about getting to the second one."},{"type":"p","text":"Below is a calm, practical way to think about it — not a rigid program, just a handful of ideas you can borrow tonight and adjust for your own family."},{"type":"h2","text":"Cook once, eat twice"},{"type":"p","text":"Double the batch, freeze half. A little extra effort tonight buys you a free dinner on the worst night of next week — the cheapest insurance in the kitchen."},{"type":"h2","text":"Lower the stakes on dinner"},{"type":"p","text":"A simple meal eaten together beats an elaborate one served to a stressed table. The nutrition of connection is real; give yourself permission to keep it easy."},{"type":"h2","text":"Keep a short list of house dinners"},{"type":"p","text":"Every family needs ten reliable, everyone-eats-it meals on rotation. It's not boring; it's a foundation. Save the experiments for the weekend and let weeknights be easy."},{"type":"h2","text":"Get kids in the kitchen"},{"type":"p","text":"Children eat what they help make. Even a toddler can wash, tear, and stir, and the pride of \"I made this\" does more for picky eating than any bribe."},{"type":"h2","text":"Prep components, not full meals"},{"type":"p","text":"Cooked grains, roasted veg, and a protein in the fridge become five different dinners. Prepping building blocks beats cooking five separate meals and keeps leftovers from feeling like leftovers."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, put it somewhere the whole family can see it. Next, add a gentle reminder so nobody has to hold it in their head. Then, give it two weeks before you judge whether it's working."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"This is exactly the kind of invisible work Bubaly was built for. Instead of holding the picky-eater-friendly stir-fry in your head, you hand it to your family's shared system — Bubaly turns plans into real calendar events, reminders, lists, and gentle nudges, so the whole household stays in sync. Explore it at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"The goal was never a flawless household. It's a calmer one — and that's absolutely within reach."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
('a-five-minute-weeknight-salad-small-changes-big-difference', 'A Five-minute Weeknight Salad: Small Changes, Big Difference', 'If a five-minute weeknight salad has ever turned an ordinary evening into a low-grade negotiation, you are in excellent company. We''ll walk through what actually moves the needle, ', 'Hannah Cho', '2025-03-12', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familymeals','#fiveminuteweeknight','#parentinghacks','#raisingkids']::text[], 'Recipes & Food', false, '#f97316', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"If a five-minute weeknight salad has ever turned an ordinary evening into a low-grade negotiation, you are in excellent company."},{"type":"p","text":"We'll walk through what actually moves the needle, what to skip, and how to make it feel less like a chore and more like a shared routine."},{"type":"h2","text":"Prep components, not full meals"},{"type":"p","text":"Cooked grains, roasted veg, and a protein in the fridge become five different dinners. Prepping building blocks beats cooking five separate meals and keeps leftovers from feeling like leftovers."},{"type":"h2","text":"Snacks with a plan"},{"type":"p","text":"Grazing derails appetites and budgets. A visible, pre-portioned snack shelf the kids can reach ends the constant asking and keeps dinner the main event."},{"type":"h2","text":"Get kids in the kitchen"},{"type":"p","text":"Children eat what they help make. Even a toddler can wash, tear, and stir, and the pride of \"I made this\" does more for picky eating than any bribe."},{"type":"h2","text":"Plan around the week you actually have"},{"type":"p","text":"The best dinner plan bends to reality: fast meals on busy nights, the ambitious one on a night you're home. Matching a five-minute weeknight salad to the real calendar is why plans survive past Wednesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Leftovers, reinvented"},{"type":"p","text":"Last night's roast chicken is tonight's tacos and tomorrow's soup. Treating leftovers as ingredients, not repeats, slashes waste and the mental load at once."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, start smaller than feels necessary — momentum beats ambition. Next, write down the plan so it survives a chaotic day. Then, agree on who owns it so it isn't quietly one person's job."},{"type":"h2","text":"Where Bubaly fits in"},{"type":"p","text":"Want a five-minute weeknight salad to run itself? That's what Bubaly does — one calm home for your family's schedule, tasks, meals, and money, with AI that stays a step ahead. Start at bubaly.com."},{"type":"p","text":"Start small, stay consistent, and let the system do the remembering so you don't have to."}]$json$::jsonb, true),
