('the-reliable-family-chili-made-easy', 'The Reliable Family Chili, Made Easy', 'There''s a version of the reliable family chili that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough t', 'Nina Patel', '2025-08-07', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familymeals','#reliablefamily','#worklifebalance','#momlife']::text[], 'Recipes & Food', false, '#f97316', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"There's a version of the reliable family chili that feels like a fight, and a version that feels like a rhythm. This is about getting to the second one."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Leftovers, reinvented"},{"type":"p","text":"Last night's roast chicken is tonight's tacos and tomorrow's soup. Treating leftovers as ingredients, not repeats, slashes waste and the mental load at once."},{"type":"h2","text":"Keep a short list of house dinners"},{"type":"p","text":"Every family needs ten reliable, everyone-eats-it meals on rotation. It's not boring; it's a foundation. Save the experiments for the weekend and let weeknights be easy."},{"type":"h2","text":"The list builds itself"},{"type":"p","text":"A meal plan and a grocery list are the same document. Write the plan, and the list falls out of it — sorted by aisle, minus what's already in the pantry."},{"type":"h2","text":"A well-stocked pantry is a safety net"},{"type":"p","text":"When the fridge looks empty, a good pantry still has dinner in it. A handful of staples — pasta, beans, tinned tomatoes, rice — means you're never truly stuck."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simple place to start"},{"type":"p","text":"First, start smaller than feels necessary — momentum beats ambition. Next, give it two weeks before you judge whether it's working. Then, put it somewhere the whole family can see it."},{"type":"h2","text":"