('how-to-handle-the-airport-day-with-kids-and-actually-enjoy-it', 'How to Handle The Airport Day with Kids (and Actually Enjoy It)', 'Most families don''t struggle with the airport day with kids because they''re doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system. What follows is the approach we keep', 'The Bubaly Team', '2026-03-07', 3, ARRAY['#bubaly','#familylife','#familytravel','#airportwith','#homelife','#familyfirst']::text[], 'Travel & Adventures', false, '#06b6d4', null, null, null, $json$[{"type":"p","text":"Most families don't struggle with the airport day with kids because they're doing it wrong — they struggle because nobody handed them a system."},{"type":"p","text":"What follows is the approach we keep coming back to: simple enough to start this week, flexible enough to survive a bad Tuesday."},{"type":"h2","text":"Plan for the weather you'll get"},{"type":"p","text":"A backup indoor idea and a rain layer turn a washout into a pivot. The families who \"get lucky\" with weather are usually just the ones who planned for it."},{"type":"h2","text":"Ease back in"},{"type":"p","text":"The re-entry is part of the trip. An unpacking plan and a buffer day before real life resumes keeps the vacation glow from evaporating in a Monday-morning scramble."},{"type":"h2","text":"The adventure can be small"},{"type":"p","text":"A memorable outing doesn't require a passport. A new park, a sunrise pancake run, a night hike with flashlights — the airport day with kids is really about attention, not distance."},{"type":"h2","text":"Keep the routine anchors"},{"type":"p","text":"Even on the road, a familiar bedtime book or morning ritual keeps young kids regulated. A few portable anchors let everything else be an adventure."},{"type":"h2","text":"Document lightly, live fully"},{"type":"p","text":"A handful of real photos beats a phone glued to your face all day. Capture a moment, then put it away and actually be in the next one."},{"type":"h2","text":"A simp